    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWhen a registered quantization method is unsupported on CPU, `get_quantization_config` rejects it, but the error says \"Available methods on CPU\" while interpolating every key of `QUANTIZATION_METHODS`. The message therefore advertises methods CPU cannot run, including the one just rejected. For example, `awq_marlin` on CPU is rejected, yet listed as available.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Build the CPU validation message from `CPU_QUANTIZATION_METHODS` instead of `QUANTIZATION_METHODS`.\n- Add a regression test in `test/registered/unit/configs/test_quant_config_parsing.py` that forces the CPU branch (patching only `is_cpu` and `cpu_has_amx_support`) and asserts the exception lists exactly `CPU_QUANTIZATION_METHODS`.\n\nOnly the error text changes; method registration and CPU support are untouched.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: error-message text only.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: rejection path only.\n\n## Testing\n\n- The new test fails on `main` (the message lists the non-CPU methods) and passes with the fix.\n- `pytest test/registered/unit/configs`: 96 passed.\n- `pre-commit run` on both changed files: passed.\n\nRelated to #31783.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang 